# Equipment that a meter measures but nothing declared (BUG-249, found 2026-08-27).
#
# bldg2.ttl carries `bldg:Wellman_ChilledWater_Demand_kBtu brick:isPointOf bldg:chiller`
# against a subject declared in no file. The meter is evidence that a chiller exists --
# something is being metered -- so the honest repair is to declare it, not to delete the
# meter's only statement about what it measures.
#
# Type and label only. No capacity, no location, no feeds: the source dataset says
# nothing about any of those, and a plausible guess is how a graph starts asserting
# things nobody measured.

@prefix bldg: <http://buildsys.org/ontologies/bldg2#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix brick:<https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#> .

bldg:chiller a brick:Chiller ;
    rdfs:label "Chiller" ;
    rdfs:comment "Declared because a chilled-water demand meter names it as the equipment it measures; the source dataset declares nothing further about it." .
